2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] Yes, with Anthropic's file API you can share source files as plain text! The API supports various
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] text-based file formats including:
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - Source code files (.js, .py, .java, .cpp, etc.)
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - Plain text files (.txt)
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - Markdown files (.md)
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - JSON, XML, YAML files
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - Shell scripts and config files
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] When you upload these files through the API, they're treated as text content that can be read and
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] processed. The files are included in the conversation context, so you can ask questions about the
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] code, request modifications, or have the AI analyze the content.
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] The main limitations are:
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - File size limits (varies by API tier)
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - Binary files aren't supported - only text-based formats
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] - Total context window limits still apply
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] This makes it convenient for sharing entire codebases, documentation, or configuration files
2025-08-06 13:35:03 [claude-opus-4] without having to copy-paste everything into the message.
