2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] Looking at your updated code, I can see the Anthropic tool calling issue more clearly now. The
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] problem is in the `connectAnthropic` function around lines 1013-1047. Here's what's happening:
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] The Issues
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] 1. Undefined variables: You're referencing `calls`, `choice`, `verbose`, `depth`,
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] `payload`, and `mut` that don't exist in this scope.
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] 2. Incorrect tool execution flow: The tool handling code is copied from the main relay
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] function but doesn't match Anthropic's format.
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] 3. Missing tool conversation loop: Claude needs to see the tool results and continue the
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] conversation internally.
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] The Fix
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] Here's how to handle Anthropic tools natively within the connector:
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] // Inside connectAnthropic's create function:
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] create: async (payload) => {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     const model = payload.model;
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     const system = anthropicSystem(payload);
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     const temperature = grokTemperature;
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     const max_tokens = 2048;
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     let messages = await anthropicMessages(sdk, payload);
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     let totalUsage = { input_tokens: 0, output_tokens: 0 };
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     while (true) {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         const request = { model, max_tokens, temperature, system, messages };
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         if (payload.tools) {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             request.tools = anthropicTools(payload);
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         const options = { headers: { "anthropic-beta": "files-api-2025-04-14" } };
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         const reply = await sdk.messages.create(request, options);
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         // Accumulate usage
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         totalUsage.input_tokens += reply.usage.input_tokens;
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         totalUsage.output_tokens += reply.usage.output_tokens;
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         if (reply.stop_reason === "tool_use") {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             // Add Claude's message with tool calls to conversation
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             messages.push({ role: "assistant", content: reply.content });
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             // Execute tools and add results
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             const toolResults = [];
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             for (const content of reply.content) {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                 if (content.type === "tool_use") {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                     const toolCall = {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                         id: content.id,
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                         function: {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                             name: content.name,
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                             arguments: JSON.stringify(content.input)
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                         }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                     };
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                     const result = await onCall(toolCall);
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                     toolResults.push({
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                         type: "tool_result",
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                         tool_use_id: content.id,
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                         content: JSON.stringify(result)
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                     });
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]                 }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             // Add tool results as user message
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             messages.push({ role: "user", content: toolResults });
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             // Continue the loop to get Claude's final response
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             continue;
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         // Final response - return it
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         const content = reply.content[0]?.text || "";
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         const choices = [{ message: { content } }];
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         const usage = {
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             prompt_tokens: totalUsage.input_tokens,
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]             completion_tokens: totalUsage.output_tokens
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         };
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]         return { model, choices, usage };
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4]     }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] }
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] This approach keeps the tool execution loop entirely within the Anthropic connector and returns
2025-08-06 16:21:53 [claude-sonnet-4] only the final response to the main relay, avoiding the recursive complexity and format mismatches.
