2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Machine Readability of Mathematical Digits (`𝟬-𝟵`)
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] - OCR/Text Parsing: Most modern OCR (like Tesseract) and parsers (regex, etc.) can
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] recognize these Unicode digits, but:
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat]   - Slower processing (vs. ASCII `0-9`)
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat]   - May require explicit Unicode support in libraries
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] - Databases/APIs: Some systems may treat them as "special characters" rather than numerals.
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] - Accessibility: Screen readers usually read them as numbers, but testing is
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] advised.
2025-08-08 22:21:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Use Case: Hexadecimal with Bold Sans (`𝗔𝗕𝗖𝗗𝗘𝗙` + `𝟬-𝟵`)
