2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Hair space is U+200A. In JS/TS you can write it as "\u200A" or "\u{200A}".
2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Example replacement: const thinSpace = "\u200A";
2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] Other useful ones:
2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Thin space: U+2009 => "\u2009"
2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Narrow no‑break space: U+202F => "\u202F"
2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] Note: ensure your source file is UTF‑8. Some renderers still collapse very narrow spaces, so use
2025-08-13 11:21:15 [gpt-5-mini] U+2009 or U+202F if you need a reliably visible narrow gap.
