2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Pick a voice: run in Terminal
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini]   - say -v ?
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini]   - (Siri-like built‑in voices include Alex, Samantha, Victoria, etc. — check output)
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Speak immediately (no code):
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini]   - say -v "Samantha" "Hello from Deno"
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Save speech to a file and convert to mp3 (if needed):
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini]   - say -v "Samantha" -o speech.aiff "Hello"
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini]   - ffmpeg -i speech.aiff -b:a 192k speech.mp3
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] Minimal Deno example (run with --allow-run --allow-write):
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] 	tab://
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] 	const text = "Hello from Deno and macOS speech";
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] 	await Deno.run({ cmd: ["say", "-v", "Samantha", text] }).status();
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] To save to file and convert inside Deno (requires ffmpeg installed):
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] 	tab://
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] 	await Deno.run({ cmd: ["say", "-v", "Samantha", "-o", "speech.aiff", "Hello"] }).status();
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] 	await Deno.run({ cmd: ["ffmpeg", "-y", "-i", "speech.aiff", "speech.mp3"] }).status();
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] Notes:
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] - Siri-branded voices may not expose the literal name "Siri" — use `say -v ?` to find the closest
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] voice on your macOS version.
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] - No network or extra API keys required. Deno must be run with --allow-run and --allow-write (and
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] --allow-read if you read files).
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] - For programmatic low-latency/streaming or fine controls, consider AVSpeechSynthesizer via a small
2025-08-13 13:53:15 [gpt-5-mini] native helper (AppleScript/Swift) — but `say` covers most simple cases.
