2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] Ah, the classic "partial wipe" issue with emoji/wide chars! Here’s why this happens and how to fix
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] it:
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] Root Cause
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] 1. Column Misalignment
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat]    - Emoji (e.g., ❤️) often use 2 terminal columns, but naive backspace (`\x08`) only moves
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] the cursor back 1 column.
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat]    - Result: The right half of the emoji remains visible after deletion.
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] 2. ANSI Sequence Gaps
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat]    - Your current `backspace()` sends `[0x08, 0x20, 0x08]` (backspace + space + backspace).
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat]    - This works for 1-column chars but fails for 2-column-wide emoji.
2025-08-17 17:30:03 [deepseek-chat] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
