2025-08-22 11:10:30 [simon@midnightblue] slop prompt is using streaming decoder no?
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] Short answer: yes — you create a streaming TextDecoder (decoderStream) — but the way you use it
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] defeats most of the benefit.
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] Why it can still corrupt paste/emoji:
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - You decode one byte at a time (decoderStream.decode(new Uint8Array([byte]))). A streaming decoder
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] will buffer incomplete multibyte sequences and often return an empty string until the sequence is
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] complete. your code treats an empty result as a failure/ignores it (logs "[RAW] not char …" /
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] breaks), so bytes get dropped or mishandled.
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - You iterate incoming chunks per-byte instead of decoding the whole chunk. multibyte UTF‑8 (emoji,
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] accented characters) can arrive inside a single chunk or be split across chunks; decoding the whole
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] chunk preserves sequences.
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - You decode → then re-encode per-char (encoder.encode(char)) and write that — doubling work and
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] increasing chance of subtle changes (combining marks, ZWJ sequences).
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] What to do:
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - Decode the entire chunk at once: const s = decoderStream.decode(value /, { stream: true } if
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] needed/); then iterate grapheme clusters from s (segmenter) and push them to grapheme.
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - Don’t break/throw on empty decode results — let the streaming decoder buffer until a full
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] sequence is available.
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - When writing to stdout, write the decoded string (or the original chunk) instead of re-encoding
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] each char.
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] - Handle colon/shortcode logic over grapheme clusters (not bytes).
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] If you want, I can show the minimal patch to sloprawprompt.ts to decode whole chunks and process
2025-08-22 11:10:57 [gpt-5-mini] graphemes.
